WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.182
Graph neural networks are increasingly deployed in
safety-critical settings,

00:00:04.262 --> 00:00:08.444
but their confidence estimates often become
unreliable when the test data shifts away from training.

00:00:08.524 --> 00:00:12.706
This paper,

00:00:12.786 --> 00:00:16.968
from the University of Michigan and Lawrence
Livermore National Laboratory,

00:00:17.048 --> 00:00:21.230
introduces G-Delta-UQ,

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:25.492
a single-model method for estimating epistemic
uncertainty in graph neural networks.

00:00:25.572 --> 00:00:29.754
By adapting stochastic centering and partial
stochasticity to structured graph data,

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:34.016
G-Delta-UQ produces better-calibrated confidence
indicators across size, concept,

00:00:34.096 --> 00:00:38.278
and covariate distribution shifts,

00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:42.540
and improves downstream tasks like
out-of-distribution detection and generalization gap prediction.
